# Slidesmith is bring-your-own-keys. The easiest way to configure it is the
# in-app Settings screen — keys are saved to ~/.slidesmith/config.json.
#
# These env vars are optional overrides for self-hosting / headless setups:

# Port the local Slidesmith server listens on (default 8787).
# PORT=8787

# Interface to bind (default 127.0.0.1 — loopback only). DO NOT expose it to a
# network unless you're behind a firewall (or have set APP_PASSWORD below)
# and know what you're doing.
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# Where config + the generation queue are stored (default ~/.slidesmith).
# SLIDESMITH_DIR=/path/to/data

# You do NOT need to put API keys here — enter them in Settings instead.
# (post-bridge key for scheduling/posting/analytics, OpenRouter key for the AI.)
#
# Optional: set a key here instead if you want it to survive regardless of
# where config is stored — e.g. on Vercel, where local config files don't
# persist across cold starts. An env var here always wins over whatever's
# saved in Settings.
# POSTBRIDGE_API_KEY=pb_...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# APIFY_API_KEY=apify_api_...

# ── Reddit (for the Reddit / Subreddit tools) ─────────────────────────────────
# Reddit blocks anonymous .json requests from datacenter IPs (Vercel) and,
# increasingly, from home IPs too — so reading a post's commenters or a sub's
# rules/top posts needs the OAuth API. Create a "script" app at
# https://www.reddit.com/prefs/apps (pick "script", any name, redirect URI
# http://localhost:8787), then fill these in. Copy this file to .env — the
# local server auto-loads it (see server/env.js). On Vercel, set the same vars
# in Project → Settings → Environment Variables instead.
# REDDIT_CLIENT_ID=your_app_client_id
# REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET=your_app_secret
# REDDIT_USERNAME=your_reddit_username
# REDDIT_PASSWORD=your_reddit_password
# REDDIT_USER_AGENT=SlideSmith/1.0 by /u/your_reddit_username

# ── Deploying somewhere public (Vercel) ───────────────────────────────────────
# Only relevant if you're deploying Slidesmith so it's reachable by others —
# see "Deploying somewhere public (Vercel)" in the README. Not needed for
# local self-hosting.

# Requires anyone using the deployment to enter this password once before the
# app (and therefore your API keys) is reachable at all. Strongly recommended
# for any public deployment.
# APP_PASSWORD=choose-a-shared-password
